A '''Lady''' (Japanese: '''おじょうさま''' ''High-class Girl'') is a type of [[Pokémon Trainer]] that first debuted in the [[Generation III]] games. They are depicted as girls dressed in elaborate and fancy clothing. In {{game|Platinum}}, {{2v2|HeartGold|SoulSilver}}, [[Caitlin]] is referred to as a Lady. In {{2v2|FireRed|LeafGreen}}, a notable Lady is [[Selphy]]. Their male counterparts are {{tc|Rich Boy}}s.

They generally use weak {{OBP|Pokémon|species}} but pay out a large amount of [[Pokémon Dollar|money]] as a reward; the largest recorded [[prize money]] after a Trainer battle was {{PDollar}}10,240, which can be multiplied to {{PDollar}}20,480 with an [[Amulet Coin]] or [[Luck Incense]]. Many of their Pokémon also carry [[Nugget]]s or [[Stardust]] in the Generation III main series games. They use [[Full Restore]]s to heal their own Pokémon in battle.

In {{pkmn|X and Y}}, they appear in the [[Battle Chateau]], where they appear as a {{tc|Baroness}}, {{tc|Viscountess}}, {{tc|Countess}}, {{tc|Marchioness}} or {{tc|Duchess}}. They also appear in the [[Battle Maison]], meaning there are no Ladies that can be battled outside of the Battle Maison.

